{{Quote|Chh-chh. Clem; Grakata|[[Clem]], reunited with his weapons of choice}}
The '''Twin Grakatas''' are the akimbo secondary variant of the primary {{Weapon|Grakata}} assault rifle. Despite its lackluster base damage, it possesses a very high [[critical chance]], [[critical multiplier]] and extreme [[fire rate]], making this weapon deceptively powerful. It also fires two bullets at once due to its innate [[multishot]], but in turn, it depletes its high ammo pool alarmingly quickly. It is also [[Clem]]'s weapon of choice and are also used by [[Eviscerator|Emperyan Evicirators]].

==Characteristics==
* This weapon deals primarily {{D|Impact}} damage.
* Innate [[multishot]] of 2 bullets, and consumes 2 ammo per shot.
** Functionally acts as double fire-rate.

{{Advantages|
*Innate multishot provides doubled damage output and status output.
*Negligible recoil.
}}

{{Disadvantages|
*Very low base damage, reliant on its high critical damage potential. Ill-suited against [[Damage/Object|Object]]-based health as it nullifies any critical hits.
*Extremely poor ammo efficiency. Further reinforced by the double consumption of ammo.
}}

==Acquisition==
The Twin Grakata's blueprint can be purchased from the [[Market]].

{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}
This weapon can be sold for {{cc|5,000}}.

==Notes==
*The Twin Grakatas fire two bullets per shot. This means that the actual fire rate is double that of the listed fire rate.
*The total credit cost of crafting the Twin Grakatas, including the blueprint and the building costs of its two constituent Grakatas, is {{cc|195,000}}.
*Compared to the Grakata, each individual bullet will deal '''4''' {{D|Impact}}, '''3.35''' {{D|Puncture}}, and '''2.65''' {{D|Slash}}, which is less damage per bullet than the Grakata, but fires two of these at once, resulting in far more DPS. The weapon also has the advantage of a much more efficient [[Hornet Strike|physical damage mod]] as well as {{M|Lethal Torrent}}, causing the Twin Grakatas to have a higher DPS.
*Mods that affect the standalone Grakata, such as {{M|Wild Frenzy}} and [[Riven Mods]], cannot be equipped on the Twin Grakatas.

==Trivia==
*The Twin Grakatas were first presented in the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?t=32&v=oAVA_vGb9_w Echoes of the Sentients Highlight Video.]
*The Twin Grakatas appear to have been inspired by [[:File:4DcB2Ct.png|a popular fan-made comic]] by ''Datareaper'' (who was the designer of the {{Weapon|Kronen}}) involving a [[Grineer]] [[Lancer]] named [[Clem]], who idolizes the Tenno and is seen wielding two Grakatas as his signature weapon.
*The Twin Grakatas are the first weapons to occupy a different weapon slot to their default counterpart - while the single Grakata is a primary weapon, the Twin Grakatas are considered secondary weapons and thus use pistol mods instead of rifle mods.
*The Twin Grakatas are the first dual-wielded version of another weapon to fire more projectiles at once instead of having increased magazine size and fire rate.
*The Twin Grakatas possess the highest possible ammo reserve (2280 with the {{M|Trick Mag}} mod) of all equippable weapons, barring Archwing weapons which have an infinite reserve.
*Tied with {{Weapon|Dual Cestra}} and {{Weapon|Secura Dual Cestra}} for the second largest magazine size of all secondaries.
*Lowest damage per bullet of all secondaries.

==Bugs==
*If the player owns a {{Weapon|Prisma Grakata}} the game will display it as an available material for building the Twin Grakatas, despite the fact that it cannot be selected.{{clr}}

