{{Codex|An artifact of exquisite beauty. A weapon of deadly purpose.}}The '''Tigris Prime''' is the [[Prime]]d variant of the {{Weapon|Tigris}} shotgun, sporting drastically higher damage and pellet count but at some expense to [[status chance]]. It was released alongside {{WF|Nekros Prime}} and {{Weapon|Galatine Prime}}.

==Characteristics==
*This weapon deals primarily {{D|Slash}} damage.
*Can use the Tigris-exclusive {{M|Combat Reload}} mod.
*Innate [[multishot]] of 8 pellets.
*Unique trigger type allows for two rapid shots against tough targets, or careful shot management against many weaker opponents. First shot on button press, the second on button release.
*Innate {{Pol|Madurai}} and {{Pol|Naramon}} polarities.

{{Advantages|class=Shotgun|
*Second highest base damage of all primary shotguns, behind {{Weapon|Exergis}}.
}}

{{Disadvantages|class=Shotgun|
*Has linear damage falloff from 100% to 51.28% from 10m to 20m target distance (distances are affected [[Projectile Speed]]).
*Inefficient against groups, unless using [[Punch Through]] mods.
*Extremely low magazine size of just two rounds; requires frequent reloading.
}}

{{WeaponComparison|Tigris}}
{{WeaponComparison|Sancti Tigris|header=n}}

==Acquisition==
{{PrimeTable}}
{{BuildAutomatic|type=Weapon}}

===Vaultings===
*On [https://forums.warframe.com/topic/963813-zephyr-prime-access-flies-away-and-nekros-prime-vaulting-on-june-19th/ June 5, 2018], it was announced that Tigris Prime, alongside {{WF|Nekros Prime}} and {{Weapon|Galatine Prime}}, would enter the Prime Vault and be retired from the reward tables on June 19, 2018. Any preexisting components or fully-built weapons will remain as is.

==Tips==
*Due to the weapon's low magazine size and tight spread, consider using {{M|Seeking Force}} and/or {{M|Seeking Fury}} in order to deal with large groups more effectively.
*{{M|Chilling Reload}} can also help to speed up the weapon's frequent reloads.
*All Tigris variants can reach 4 shells in the magazine with a rank 7 or higher {{M|Primed Ammo Stock}}.
*Aiming down sights will increase weapon accuracy and decrease shotgun spread, making the Tigris more effective at medium ranges.
*Negative Fire Rate mods such as {{M|Critical Deceleration}} will increase the delay before automatically reloading. The delay does not affect manual reloading.

